$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}x}\left(3 x^{2} \cos{\left(y \right)}\right)&=- 3 x^{2} y' \sin{\left(y \right)} + 6 x \cos{\left(y \right)}
\end{aligned}
$$

Differentiate the equation, collect all terms containing $y^{\prime}$, and factor:

$$
\begin{aligned}
6 x \cos{\left(y \right)} + y' \left(- 3 x^{2} \sin{\left(y \right)} - 3 y^{2}\right)&=9 x^{2}\\
\left(- 3 x^{2} \sin{\left(y \right)} - 3 y^{2}\right)y^{\prime}&=9 x^{2} - 6 x \cos{\left(y \right)}
\end{aligned}
$$

Divide by the coefficient of $y^{\prime}$:

$$
\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}=\frac{9 x^{2} - 6 x \cos{\left(y \right)}}{- 3 x^{2} \sin{\left(y \right)} - 3 y^{2}}
$$

This formula applies where $- 3 x^{2} \sin{\left(y \right)} - 3 y^{2}\ne0$.

Differentiate both sides with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a function $y(x)$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}x}\left(y^{2} + y\right)&=\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}x}\left(- 4 x - 2\right)\\
2 y\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}+1\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}&=-4
\end{aligned}
$$

Collect the terms containing $\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}$, factor, and solve:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\left(2 y + 1\right)\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}&=-4\\
\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}&=-\frac{4}{2 y + 1}
\end{aligned}
$$

This formula applies on real branches where $2 y + 1\ne 0$.

Differentiate both sides with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a function $y(x)$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}x}\left(y^{2} + 2 y\right)&=\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}x}\left(2 - 4 x\right)\\
2 y\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}+2\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}&=-4
\end{aligned}
$$

Collect the terms containing $\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}$, factor, and solve:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\left(2 y + 2\right)\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}&=-4\\
\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}&=-\frac{4}{2 y + 2}
\end{aligned}
$$

This formula applies on real branches where $2 y + 2\ne 0$.

Differentiate both sides with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a function $y(x)$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}x}\left(y^{2} + 2 y\right)&=\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}x}\left(4 x\right)\\
2 y\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}+2\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}&=4
\end{aligned}
$$

Collect the terms containing $\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}$, factor, and solve:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\left(2 y + 2\right)\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}&=4\\
\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}&=\frac{4}{2 y + 2}
\end{aligned}
$$

This formula applies on real branches where $2 y + 2\ne 0$.

Differentiate both sides with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a function $y(x)$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}x}\left(y^{2} - 2 y\right)&=\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}x}\left(3 x - 3\right)\\
2 y\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}-2\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}&=3
\end{aligned}
$$

Collect the terms containing $\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}$, factor, and solve:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\left(2 y - 2\right)\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}&=3\\
\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}&=\frac{3}{2 y - 2}
\end{aligned}
$$

This formula applies on real branches where $2 y - 2\ne 0$.

Differentiate both sides with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a function $y(x)$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}x}\left(y^{2} - y\right)&=\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}x}\left(4 x - 2\right)\\
2 y\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}-1\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}&=4
\end{aligned}
$$

Collect the terms containing $\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}$, factor, and solve:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\left(2 y - 1\right)\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}&=4\\
\frac{\mathrm{d}y}{\mathrm{d}x}&=\frac{4}{2 y - 1}
\end{aligned}
$$

This formula applies on real branches where $2 y - 1\ne 0$.

